<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-32--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch03-32: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.48";
    dc:description "The decision variable is a ratio of two growth rates, which experiments have sometimes recorded. There is no compiled public series, and the taxonomic scope is several heterochelous groups studied separately. Even a compiled table would leave neural and molt-stage programs as serious alternative causes of the same reversal.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: After claw amputation, measure the regenerative growth rate of the stump and the growth rate of the intact claw, and predict reversal from whether the intact claw reaches the large-claw size class first. Reversal when and only when that ratio favours the intact claw would support the claim; reversal uncorrelated with the two rates would refute it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Form-follows-size has to be granted before the rate ratio is interpreted.", "Nerve supply, molt stage and a handedness program can reverse claws at the same sizes.", "Paired rate measurements are spread across lobster, snapping-shrimp and crab papers.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.57"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.48"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-32--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of thompson1917-ch03-32 by Grok 4.7: 0.4";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
